{title: 391 - Welcome, Welcome, Day of Rest}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #391 • PLEYEL'S HYMN • 15.15}
{lyricist: Anon}
{composer: Ignace Pleyel}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 391}
{meta: tune PLEYEL'S HYMN}
{meta: meter 15.15}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Welcome, welcome, [F#dim]day [C/G]of [F#dim]rest, [G]To the world [F#dim]in kindness given;
[F#dim]Welcome [Em/B]to [Am]this [D/A]humble breast, [G]As the [F#dim]beaming [C/G]light [F#dim]from heaven.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Day [F#dim]of [C/G]calm [G]and sweet [F#dim]repose,
[G]Gently [C/G]now [G]thy moments [F#dim]run;
[F#dim]Balm [Bm]to [Am]soothe [C/G]our [G]cares [C/G]and [F#dim]woes,
[F#dim]Till [Em/B]our [D/A]labor [G]here [F#dim]is done.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Holy [C/G]day [G]that most [F#dim]we prize,
[G]Day [F#dim]of [C/G]solemn [G]praise [F#dim]and prayer,
[F#dim]Day [Em/B]to [D/A]make the [G]simple [F#dim]wise,
[F#dim]O, [Em/B]how [D/A]great thy [G]blessings [F#dim]are!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Welcome, [C/G]welcome, [G]day [F#dim]of rest,
[G]With [F#dim]thy [C/G]influence [G]all [F#dim]divine;
[F#dim]May [Em/B]thy [D/A]hallowed [G]hours [F#dim]be blessed
[F#dim]to [Em/B]this [D/A]waiting [G]heart [F#dim]of mine.
{end_of_verse}
